.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH pkgds 1  "pkgds 0.1.1" 
.SH NAME
pkgds \- Real disk usage per package for Arch Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpkgds\fR [\fB\-H \fR] [\fB\-s \fR] [\fB\-\-sort\fR] [\fB\-n\fR|\fB\-\-limit\fR] [\fB\-\-btrfs\fR] [\fB\-\-root\fR] [\fB\-\-dbpath\fR] [\fB\-d \fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-apparent\-size\fR] [\fB\-\-total\fR] [\fB\-\-files\fR] [\fB\-\-tree\fR] [\fB\-\-depth\fR] [\fB\-\-breadth\fR] [\fB\-\-min\-percent\fR] [\fB\-\-with\-deps\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIPOSITIONAL\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Real disk usage per package for Arch Linux
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-H\fR \fI<HUMANSIZE>\fR
Human\-size unit (B, K, Ki, M, Mi, G, Gi, T, Ti, auto, auto\-si)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
B
.IP \(bu 2
K
.IP \(bu 2
Ki
.IP \(bu 2
M
.IP \(bu 2
Mi
.IP \(bu 2
G
.IP \(bu 2
Gi
.IP \(bu 2
T
.IP \(bu 2
Ti
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
auto\-si
.RE
.TP
\fB\-s\fR \fI<SEARCH>\fR
Search packages by regex on name
.TP
\fB\-\-sort\fR \fI<SORT>\fR [default: real]
Sort by field: name (ascending), real (alias size)/apparent/files (descending), ratio (ascending)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
name
.IP \(bu 2
real
.IP \(bu 2
size
.IP \(bu 2
apparent
.IP \(bu 2
files
.IP \(bu 2
ratio
.RE
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-limit\fR \fI<LIMIT>\fR
Show only top N packages (0 = unlimited; default 20)
.TP
\fB\-\-btrfs\fR
Enable btrfs on\-disk size tokens (%z, %r)
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fI<ROOT>\fR [default: /]
Set filesystem root prefix
.TP
\fB\-\-dbpath\fR \fI<DBPATH>\fR
Override pacman local DB path (absolute)
.TP
\fB\-d\fR \fI<DELIM>\fR
Delimiter between packages in format mode (default: newline)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Show warnings for missing files, permission errors
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable color output
.TP
\fB\-\-apparent\-size\fR
Show apparent file size instead of disk blocks (du \-\-apparent\-size)
.TP
\fB\-\-total\fR
Show total row at the bottom of table output
.TP
\fB\-\-files\fR
Show file count column
.TP
\fB\-\-tree\fR
Show a per\-package file/dir tree (default depth 1)
.TP
\fB\-\-depth\fR \fI<DEPTH>\fR
Tree depth in levels (implies \-\-tree; default 1)
.TP
\fB\-\-breadth\fR \fI<BREADTH>\fR
Show at most K children per directory (default 5; requires \-\-tree)
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-percent\fR \fI<MIN_PERCENT>\fR
Prune entries below this percentage of their parent (requires \-\-tree; default 0.1)
.TP
\fB\-\-with\-deps\fR
Also include the dependencies that removing the target(s) would free
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
[\fIPOSITIONAL\fR]
Format string (printf\-style) or package names

Flags may follow package names (`pkgds bash \-\-btrfs`). A format string that starts with `\-` therefore needs the `\-\-` separator.
.SH VERSION
v0.1.1
